  "execution_policy": [
    "Validate integrity immediately before one selected foreground command, enforcing its timeout. No unattended batch.",
    "All executing campaign Python components are individually hash-bound to raw content-addressed snapshots, not only an opaque source manifest.",
    "Native CRM executor snapshots components, executes active files, and checks unchanged bytes. Scheduler evidence executor runs archived components.",
    "Legacy fixtures and oracles must not be model input. Cases 001 and 003 lack complete separated comparison inputs.",
    "Historical preservation manifests contain superseded active hashes and sometimes case-relative paths; do not reinterpret them as current source selections.",
    "Integrity validation does not rerun suites or establish model performance. Original access is optional for bounded B1/B2 evaluation and required for parity claims."
  ],
